 ## Backend Selection
 
+Devin (`devin`) runs through its sealed per-process ACP permission bridge.
+SessionStart proves the hook on creation/load, and every PreToolUse waits for
+Crew's standard permission decision with complete arguments. Native persistent
+and bypass options are never selected. Models and thought levels use advertised
+config options; native sessions resume by id. The mirror supplies the filtered
+MCP array. Deployment restrictions and verification are in
+[harness-onboarding](harness-onboarding.md#devin-experimental-backend).
+
+
 `AcpSessionHandle.active_agent` records the mode named by session configuration,
 a completed mode handshake or an observed agent-switch event. A queued mode
 request clears that observation until confirmation. `AcpSessionProvider` exposes
