+
+## Devin experimental backend
+
+`ACP_BACKEND_DEVIN` (`devin`) is selectable in the public baseline. It runs native
+Devin CLI through a dedicated ACP bridge in
+`agent_sdk/gate_extensions/devin/bridge.py`; `acp/harness/devin.py` owns its launch.
+The CLI release verified by the bridge is **3000.12.17**. A different release is
+refused until the lifecycle-hook contract is measured on it. The native wire
+identity is `affogato`, version `0.0.0-dev`, independently of the CLI release.
+
+### Permission route
+
+Routing is `VERIFIED_GATE_EXTENSION`, with a load-marker read-back over the
+bridge's private loopback socket. The bridge and hook are package data pinned by
+SHA-256, normalized to LF and sealed with the existing owner-only `pi-gate`
+artifact machinery. The native config is read-only under that same seal. Its
+`SessionStart` and `PreToolUse` hooks run Crew's sealed Python hook; other config
+imports are disabled, and a separate native config root excludes global hooks,
+user plugins and native MCP configuration.
+
+Before a new or loaded session is acknowledged, its `SessionStart` callback must
+arrive with the bridge's private token and the exact sealed hook path. Every tool
+then waits in `PreToolUse` for a standard ACP `session/request_permission` decision
+from Crew. A complete nonce-bound gate envelope carries the native call id, tool
+identity, kind and arguments into Crew's existing parser, HookManager, governance
+and audit path. Shell/file built-ins use Crew's policy vocabulary. Denial or a
+broken permission channel returns a native blocking decision; the socket deadline
+is shorter than Devin's hook timeout, whose native error behavior is fail-open.
+
+The bridge offers only allow-once and reject-once. Crew can maintain its own trust
+policy, but native persistent permission and switch-to-bypass choices never reach
+the operator or get selected. A native follow-up approval is allowed once only
+when that same session/tool id was allowed by Crew's hook. A completed tool that
+was unasked or denied fails the bridge closed. Cancellation rejects pending hooks;
+shutdown reaps the bridge's child through `platform_compat`. A native lifecycle
+receipt for execution of the exact sealed hook command is suppressed as hook
+telemetry, not treated as a model tool; every other completion keeps the same
+per-call approval check. Raw stdin fd reads avoid a buffered-reader shutdown lock.
+
+Native `.devin` config/hook/MCP/plugin files in the workspace or its ancestors
+refuse this harness, at launch, creation/load, prompt admission and hook handling.
+This restriction belongs only to Devin. No Kiro sandbox fence is widened and
+Devin never delegates away Crew's OS sandbox or compensating credential mask.
+
+### Models, tools and persistence
+
+The `model` and `thought_level` ACP config options drive the model and effort
+controls. Account-advertised models are cached in the separate `devin` namespace;
+no concrete model is made the default. Devin's own session store handles
+`session/load`, and conversation recall survives restarting the ACP process.
+Shared-process pooling, steering, read-only Side Chat, manual compaction and
+native slash-command parity are not granted. Bot saved specs are confirmed
+against the exact consumed MCP projection before prompting, on creation and
+resume. A Bot worker resolves its per-session merged spec and receives its
+prompt through the ordinary context block. Unsupported per-tool restrictions
+and worker hooks/settings are refused by the existing capability gates.
+
+`providers/mirrors/devin.py` projects the spec's servers and pooled stubs through
+the standard ACP MCP array. It uses the shared allowlist and placement functions.
+A server narrowed per tool is withheld whole, including Crew's control plane;
+there is no claim of native per-tool deny projection. Spec hooks, resources and
+`toolsSettings` are explicitly withheld rather than silently claimed as delivered.
+
+Devin signs in separately with `devin auth login` / `devin auth status`. Its
+`~/.local/share/devin/credentials.toml` joins the credential floor and is spared
+only for its own child. As on the other file-authenticated enforced harnesses,
+that vendor's own token is readable by its process tree; other vendor stores
+remain masked. The install probe resolves `devin` or `DEVIN_BIN` and does not read
+credentials or equate installed with signed in.
+
+### Bot control-plane authentication
+
+Devin joins the member capability, dispatch, panel and worker-kit sets. Its
+host-derived `kirocrew-core`, `kirocrew-cron`, `kirocrew-dashboard` and
+`kirocrew-panel` elements use `acp/harness/devin_mcp.py`. The existing IPC issuer
+hands each its own one-time pickup, bound to this session's token and runtime
+pid; the wrapper redeems it and runs the ordinary server in the same process.
+No gateway secret is exposed and no third-party element gets a pickup. Other
+backends retain their existing issuance and launch behavior. Failed redemption
+never grants access. Per-tool-disabled servers remain withheld whole.
+
+The Bot harness picker/save validator and worker selector derive their entries
+from the capability sets, so a Devin pin uses the ordinary selection gate. This
+experimental integration is maintained as a downstream patch for reuse; it makes
+no claim of upstream support.
+
+### Verification and keeping the patch separate
+
+`test/test_devin_saved_spec.py` verifies Bot selection, consumed saved-spec
+confirmation, edited-after-save refusal and worker projection.
+`test/test_devin_member_ipc_e2e.py` runs the real Bot MCP servers under Devin
+credential masking against an authenticated loopback gateway and verifies
+successful status and panel calls. `scripts/probe_devin_member.py` is an opt-in
+real Devin/AcpClient smoke with a disposable gateway/spec, real signed session
+identity, saved-spec confirmation, once-only approvals, shell rejection and
+resume. It uses existing Devin authentication and never edits the operator's
+Bot configuration. `scripts/drive_devin_gate.py` also uses a disposable config
+and worker echo server; only scenario-specific tool names are approved. Raw
+recordings stay private until their inputs and identifiers are reviewed.
+
+`test/test_acp_backend_devin.py` verifies the full-input permission envelope,
+allow-once/reject behavior, rejection of native bypass/persistent choices, missing
+hook and unasked-completion tripwires, package digests and project-config refusal.
+`test/fixtures/acp_frames/devin/` preserves anonymized native ACP captures. The
+Dashboard uses the existing registry-driven selector and capability card; its
+selection test verifies the ordinary config PATCH. A live `AcpClient` under Crew's
+OS sandbox verifies that a rejected shell leaves no marker and an allowed shell
+creates it. `scripts/probe_devin_acp.py --mcp` is an explicit native protocol smoke
+probe for handshake, advertised models, fixed echo and restart/recall; it is not
+run by the offline suite and is separate from the Crew permission-path tests.
+
+Keep the adapter, sealed hook/bridge, mirror and Devin tests as additive files.
+Shared edits are existing registry memberships, packaging, exports and owning
+specs. Export the complete change as a binary-capable git patch and check it with
+`git apply --reverse --check` against the changed tree. After upstream updates,
+apply with `git apply --3way` and review registry/spec conflicts; no script blindly
+rewrites upstream files. Commit and push only when the operator asks.
